{"id":"chatcmpl-f561e6d8-0f09-43db-8a43-a58251b63cd5","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245540,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a visual question asks to distinguish between left vs right findings, the key challenge is resolving laterality rather than detecting the abnormality itself. Successful strategies combine independent visual-question-answering assessments with explicit spatial grounding of the candidate phrase to confirm which side of the image corresponds to the patient's anatomy. Cross-checking multiple tools and grounding the specific option phrase resolves ambiguity when a single model gives an unhelpful or null result.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by laterality (left vs right), prioritize tools that explicitly report patient-side vs image-side mapping rather than relying on a single detection model.\",\n    \"When one visual model returns a null/negative finding, escalate to independent models and phrase-grounding to triangulate the answer instead of accepting the null.\",\n    \"Ground the exact candidate phrase from each option to verify it localizes to the correct anatomical side before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Use a grounded report with original-image coordinates as a verification layer to confirm presence and laterality of the described finding.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging VQA\": \"For laterality questions, always confirm patient-left vs image-right mapping; combine a detection model, an independent VQA model, and phrase grounding for consensus.\",\n    \"Multi-option visual discrimination\": \"When options are near-identical except for one attribute (side, location), isolate that attribute and test it directly with a grounding or localization tool.\",\n    \"Tool-orchestration under uncertainty\": \"If a primary tool returns negative or ambiguous output, chain alternate tools and use the most spatially explicit evidence to break ties.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the laterality convention: does the tool report patient side or image side, and does it match the option wording?\",\n    \"Verify the chosen finding is supported by at least two independent sources (e.g., VQA + phrase grounding) before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":613,"total_tokens":1018,"completion_tokens":405,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":613},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":405}}}